    2  A   ablation_onset           0.969    83.99   2.481e+06  stylized
          Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on
          (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's
          light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~84 km as low-confidence.
          Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin,
          volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
    3  Y   first_yield              3.216    46.77   1.022e+09  physical
          Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 0.5 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and
          heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5
          / H_f in [R22]).
    4  F   flare                    3.282    45.67   3.031e+09  stylized
          Light rises x18.4 in 0.20 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated
          with: yield gen 0 at 46.7 km (99% of m0); split gen 0 at 44.8 km (99% of m0); yield gen 1 at
          43.9 km (38% of m0). Dust groups supply 77% of the rise and 73% of the light at the end of
          the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come
          from the model's deterministic cascade.
    5  B   first_breakup            3.333    44.83   6.037e+09  stylized
          Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as
          dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of
          a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification.
          Light grew x5.9 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
    6  P   peak                     3.766    37.86   7.236e+10  physical
          Maximum light. It sits ~+1.6 km from the peak of energy deposition (36.2 km) because the
          luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 16.6 km/s).
    7  b   bump                     3.767    37.85   7.187e+10  stylized
          Small fluctuation, 29% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 2) at 37.7 km. The
          fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive
          of a real event.
    8  -   drag_overtakes_ablation   3.987    34.67   4.607e+10  stylized
          Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio
          ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14
          km/s (from the model's heating law).
